Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: Guard Windows current_zone() on _WIN32_WINNT

GCC 16 added a Windows implementation of std::chrono::current_zone()
(libstdc++-v3 ChangeLog-2025, 2025-07-15, PR libstdc++/108409).  It calls
GetDynamicTimeZoneInformation(), which mingw-w64 only declares for
_WIN32_WINNT >= 0x0600 (Windows Vista).

This toolchain configures the mingw-w64 headers with
--with-default-win32-winnt=0x0400, so building libstdc++ fails with:

  tzdb.cc: In function 'std::string_view
    std::chrono::{anonymous}::detect_windows_zone()':
  tzdb.cc:2198:11: error: 'GetDynamicTimeZoneInformation' was not declared
    in this scope; did you mean 'GetTimeZoneInformation'?

libstdc++ only raises _WIN32_WINNT to 0x0600 itself when the win32 gthreads
model is used (see GLIBCXX_CHECK_GTHREADS in acinclude.m4); with
--enable-threads=single that does not happen and the new code is compiled
against whatever the target defaults to.

Compile the Windows zone detection only when the targeted Windows version
actually provides the API.  When it does not, current_zone() falls through
to the UTC default that the generic code already uses when no zone can be
determined.  Everything else in <chrono>, including locate_zone() and the
lookup of the tzdata files next to the loaded module, is unaffected.

This is a no-op for the usual _WIN32_WINNT >= 0x0600 builds.

Not submitted upstream yet; upstream master still has the unguarded call.

--- a/libstdc++-v3/src/c++20/tzdb.cc
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/src/c++20/tzdb.cc
@@ -55,6 +55,12 @@
 # include <psapi.h>
 
 # include <array>
+
+// Detecting the current time zone uses GetDynamicTimeZoneInformation, which
+// mingw-w64 only declares when targeting Windows Vista or later.
+# if !defined _WIN32_WINNT || _WIN32_WINNT >= 0x0600
+#  define _GLIBCXX_USE_WINDOWS_CURRENT_ZONE 1
+# endif
 #endif
 
 #if defined __GTHREADS && ATOMIC_POINTER_LOCK_FREE == 2
@@ -2190,7 +2196,7 @@
       return nullptr; // not found
     }
 
-#ifdef _GLIBCXX_HAVE_WINDOWS_H
+#ifdef _GLIBCXX_USE_WINDOWS_CURRENT_ZONE
     string_view
     detect_windows_zone() noexcept
     {
@@ -2424,10 +2430,14 @@
     // zone files in /usr/share/zoneinfo so we need to compare its contents
     // to each one until we find a match.
 
-#elif defined(_GLIBCXX_HAVE_WINDOWS_H)
+#elif defined(_GLIBCXX_USE_WINDOWS_CURRENT_ZONE)
     if (auto tz
 	= do_locate_zone(this->zones, this->links, detect_windows_zone()))
       return tz;
+#elif defined(_GLIBCXX_HAVE_WINDOWS_H)
+    // Targeting a Windows version that predates
+    // GetDynamicTimeZoneInformation, so the current zone cannot be detected.
+    // Fall through to the UTC default below.
 #else // defined(_AIX)
     // AIX stores current zone in $TZ in /etc/environment but the value
     // is typically a POSIX time zone name, not IANA zone.
